    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0674" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2479a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-26T20:00:00-05:00">November 26,
                            1941—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>783. I called in the Japanese Ambassador and Mr. Kurusu in the afternoon of
                    November 26<anchor n="1" xml:id="d486-f1"/> and gave them two documents—an oral
                        statement<anchor n="2" xml:id="d486-f2"/> and draft outline of a proposed
                    basis for a broad agreement covering the entire Pacific area.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d486-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>A summary of these documents follows in a subsequent telegram.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d486-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d486-f1" n="1" xml:id="d486-f1-content">
                <p>See memorandum of November 26, 1941, <ref target="frus1931-41v02#pg_764">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 764</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d486-f2" n="2" xml:id="d486-f2-content">
